,28.3,2013,62,104,22],[28858,35.0,2013,61,105,22],[28859,39.1,2013,64,109,25],[28860,36.2,1952,61,122,26],[28861,25.5,1966,60,128,26],[29159,40.6,2013,64,105,25],[29160,31.6,1952,65,116,27]],"links":[["Boise County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/idaho/boise-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on Boise County runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 19 grids, August to September came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle sat at 43% of normal in May to June and 184% in July to August. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 61% on the middle, and grid 28555 still holds its driest year in 1966 at 52%.</p>"}
